WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How about we kick
that case to Madeline

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.272 line:92%
and you help the deacon here

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-The...deacon?

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Dick Wickware,
but people call me "Deafy.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.444 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Telephone rings ]

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You -- you deaf?

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.850
-I could see how you'd lea
to that conclusion, but no

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.186
They call me Deafy on a count of
I hear what I want to hear

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what I want to hear
right now is

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:25.859
you've gotten a dress for
the sister of one of my runners.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:30.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.398 line:92%
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're here with
Timothy Olyphant.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a clip from
Installment 4 of "Fargo."

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Installment 4, Chapter 4
of "Fargo."

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Chapter 4.
Dick "Deafy" Wickware.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a hell of a name
for your character.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the things
we didn't see in that clip -

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.515
big fan of this character --
this character will take out -

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
Deafy will take out
little carrots,

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
carrot sticks
wrapped in paper towel.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you are just -- As far as
the acting of eating,

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are doing such a good jo
in this role.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
I appreciate you noticing.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
I worked -- I've been
doing it for a long time,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so -- I'll tell you,
it was lovely.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't come up with
the carrot thing.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Noah Hawley,
the wonderful Noah Hawley,

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:16.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I'd go to
the ends of the Earth

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.244 line:92%
to work with that guy again --

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:21.948
he had that written in the
script that my character, Deafy,

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
had carrots wrapped
as if they were, like,

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:27.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
neatly wrapped from his wife
as he cruised around

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.322 line:92%
looking for these fugitives.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then
I really appreciated it,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
because,
as a lot of actors know,

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.862 line:92%
if you eat while you're acting

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
it just makes you look lik
a better actor.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.199 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.234 line:92%
Do you have any tricks for -

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, actually,
you got something right there.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.171 line:92%
Give us a little right now

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. These --
They're not olives,

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.310 line:92%
but they're so delicious.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:50.977 size:75% position:38% line:92%
There's something --

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, I feel like
the commercial break

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.981 size:88% position:44%
was when you should have
gone and Googled that.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:58.551 size:88% position:44%
-Wasn't much of a break,
to be honest with you.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the people
and the crew knows

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:02.155 line:92%
it happened pretty quickly

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
we're just getting started

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.759 line:92%
and it's all almost over.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:13.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is just so nerve-racking,
these talk shows.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Do you get nervous?

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I don't get nervous
like, with you anymore.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.639 line:92%
Like, Bob Woodward's next,

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:23.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I might get
a little nervous with him.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you got to tell him -
I want to talk --

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the guy
you want to talk --

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why are we wasting time
talking to me?

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.482 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, that's true.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.785 size:78% position:39%
That guy wrote a book
about the president,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:36.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
he won a Pulitzer,
and, yet, here, you and I --

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.424 size:84% position:42%
Literally, we're just
chatting about nothing.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This career's --
this is bull...

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:40.760 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, come on.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, you know, obviously,
-By the way -- Wait.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:48.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell Bob --
He's going to appreciate this.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.103 line:92%
I think he'll appreciate this.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.005 line:92%
I've had this dream, and it's --

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:55.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can finish, but I'm not
going to tell him this.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Keep going.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:03:01.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's Kellyanne Conway,
Bill Barr, and Donald Trump.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
Only, in my dream,
Bill Barr is John Goodman

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:12.258 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and Donald is Buscemi

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Kellyanne Conway
is played by Jeff Bridges.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:19.666
And he's talking about how
this guy, George Conway,

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:25.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
took his rug,
and the president keeps going,

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Conway? That's your name,
Kellyanne."

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:32.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Bill keeps going,
"Donny, please."

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:35.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that's -- So I should tel
that to Bob Woodward.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Donny, you're out of
your element!"

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.118 line:92%
You know what's good about this?

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:42.322 size:78% position:39%
I saw your monologue.
This can all be cut.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:46.693 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.428 size:75% position:38%
This can all be cut.
-It's not -- No, no.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:52.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because once you thinking
things on this show can be cut

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's no telling
where you'll go.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.400 line:92%
You have to know there's a -

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I noticed, when you told me
that Bob was coming on,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
you didn't talk about
the award he won.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.507 line:92%
Go ahead and tell me that again.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:04.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Pulitzer.
-What was that that Bob won?

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:08.081 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:08.715 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hey --

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:11.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ask him how much he got for
that, by the way.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.319 line:92%
-I want to -- What's that?

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ask him how much
he got for that.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.155 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-For the Pulitzer?

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.991 line:92%
I'll say, "How much did you --

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:20.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, how much did you
get for that?"

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:20.827 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah, that was good.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like a guy
who's a little jealous?

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Well, how much
you get for that?

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:29.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-By the way,
how much you get for that?

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:30.970 line:92%
-Congrats on the Pulitzer.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must be some
pretty nice scratch, right

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, or make
him feel comfortable.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
He'll be like, "Oh, this guy
really is a knucklehead."

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he'll feel good
talking to you.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do actually genuinely
want to ask --

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.316 size:78% position:39%
end on something that
we hadn't planned on.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:46.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very sad -- Eddie Van Hale
just passed away,

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I noticed you're wearing
a Van Halen shirt.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:52.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
You obviously had this on hand
Greatest --

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.861
-I just learned that, and when I
heard the news I was like,

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, I'm breaking out
the shirt.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay."
-It's a very nice tribute.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:04:59.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
Greatest guitar player
of all time.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like the hits
just keep on coming, Seth.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
The hits just keep
on coming this year.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they really do.
-But I'll tell you something

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
As Jesus said, you can't sto
the waves from coming,

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.112 line:92%
but you can learn to surf.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I can't imagine
there's going to be

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
a better way to end
on it than that.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:19.786 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It's always a pleasure.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:22.588
I mean, I was worried we weren't
going to have the same

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
rat-a-tat chemistry
we usually have,

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.058 line:92%
but I think we put those -

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did we have it?
-I think we had it.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:29.562
-Because my daughter is righ
off camera and she's like,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.364 line:92%
"It's a little much, Dad."

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.333 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because the note I'm getting
off camera is like,

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.105 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Right now, you're here.

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:41.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe just
bring it down to here."

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know what?

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I'm going to
rescind my offer

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
to e-mail you,
and I'm gonna e-mail her,

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:49.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I do -- I would love to
have a direct line to you

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
from somebody who's, like,
in the house,

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
just for notes and stuff.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.687 line:92%
-Listen, you can -- Yeah.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, by the way, if you're
hiring, you know, let me know.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:01.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
We could do it every day.
We could just do...

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm jealous of anyone right no
with a job, Seth.

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, let me just tell you,
this interview --

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:07.700 line:92%
best work you've ever done

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.968 line:92%
The fourth season -- "Season."

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what they have
on the card.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give me a hard time here.
-Oh, my God!

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:14.374 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Sunday nights, 10:00 --

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to be
10:00 p.m. on FX,

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:17.443 line:92%
available the next day on FX

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we'll be right back
with Bob Woodward.

